d 'GRANGERSPEC': module to Granger causality tests across frequencies: Granger-causality spectra 
d
d     grangerspec provides seven tools for Granger causality in the
d frequency domain.  All series must be stationary, I(0):  the
d spectra and every test are built on stationary-VAR   
d representations, and a stable VAR (every companion root modulus
d below one) is assumed.  Difference or detrend integrated   
d series first - the article's own application passes all six
d series through the Hodrick-Prescott filter before testing - and  
d  check the Stability line of the output.     Time-domain Granger
d causality only says whether the past of a series y helps predict
d a series x	overall. The frequency-domain Granger-causality
d spectrum of Geweke (1982, 1984) instead measures the strength of
d the causal	link at each frequency, so that causality at low
d (business-cycle) and high frequencies can be distinguished.
d Inference on	  these spectra, however, is an open problem: the
d limiting distribution of the estimated spectrum under the null of
d no causality	  is unknown (Farne and Montanari 2022, Section
d 2.2). Farne and Montanari propose a bootstrap solution: they test
d each	  frequency-specific causality against the distribution of
d the median causality across frequencies computed on	
d stationary-bootstrap series that are independent by construction,
d so that the null hypothesis is stochastic independence    between
d the series.  grangerspec computes the spectra and performs this
d bootstrap test. 
d
d KW: Granger causality
d KW: frequency domain
d KW: spectrum
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260805
d
d Author: Ozan Eruygur,  Ankara Haci Bayram Veli University
d Support: email eruygur@@gmail.com
d
f grangerspec.ado
f grangerspec.sthlp
